mmSetUnitDataFolder(2) %[output:272b1cd6]
[FB,meta] = mmReadImgND("flybrain.tif");
%%
%[text] **`volumeViewer`** can only handle 3D volumes. So, we'll extract the green channel for display.
FBg = squeeze(FB(:,:,2,:)); % extract ch2
volumeViewer(FBg) % display in the Volume Viewer app

%%

%%
%[text] ### Adjusting the Volume Render
%[text] In the volumeViewer app, there is a Rendering Editor Tab.
%[text] #### Change the Rendering setting
%[text] - Compare Volume Rendering to Maximum Intensity Projection to Isosurface
%[text] - For isosurface, try modifying the isovalue. This is Surface Rendering. Notice how it looks different from Volume Rendering. \
%[text] #### Play around with the Opacity Plot
%[text] - Change the Rendering Setting back to Volume Rendering \
%[text] The Alphamap
%[text] - Try Changing the Alpha
%[text] - Notice how there is a transparency to the volume: The outside voxels are transparent, with
%[text] - Adjust the alphamap to "MRI"
%[text] -     Drag the left most point up to make the volume fully opaque
%[text] -  ![](text:image:9cf5) ![](text:image:7f3a)
%[text] - Now you see the volume as a black rectangular prism \
%[text] #### Try the other alphamaps
%[text] - CT-Bone, CT-Lung, etc. \
%[text] 
%[text] #### Adjust the color maps
%[text] - The following is "MRI" alphamap with a "Parula" color map
%[text] - ![](text:image:0607) \
%[text] #### Illumination
%[text] - What happens if you un-check "Lighting" \
%%
%[text] ### Visualize the Red Channels
%[text] Repeat the same steps for the red channel
FBr = squeeze(FB(:,:,1,:)); % extract Channel 1
volumeViewer(FBr)
%%
%[text] ### volshow
%[text] **volshow** is equivalent to imshow in that it simply renders the volume without all the bells and whistles of **volumeViewer.** 
%[text] The function **volshow** can be used to display a volume render of dataset as well. Notice that volshow embeds the display directly into the Livescript with a default blue background. 
volshow(FBg);
%%
%[text] ### Now You try
%[text] Display the Red Channel using volshow


